00:20:19,866 --> 00:20:23,000
I think some things are better
talked about in private.

555
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:23,866
...Talked about in private.

556
00:20:23,866 --> 00:20:25,166
[Talk in Private]

557
00:20:25,233 --> 00:20:28,500
[Talk in Private]
I felt a bit uncomfortable.

558
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,300
Not just a bit,

559
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:29,966
very uncomfortable.

560
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:34,100
Because being put on the spot like that
in front of so many people

561
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,133
made her really uneasy.

562
00:20:36,133 --> 00:20:36,833
[Worried that it may bother Xiaxia.]
I also noticed

563
00:20:36,866 --> 00:20:37,900
[Worried that it may bother Xiaxia.]
she didn't look happy

564
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,533
during the game.

565
00:20:39,533 --> 00:20:42,233
She kept looking up at the sky.

566
00:20:42,266 --> 00:20:44,200
I wanted to find a chance
to talk to her.

567
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:45,700
I don't wanna play.

568
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,266
You don't? Then can we talk?

569
00:20:48,266 --> 00:20:49,300
[Getting a Chance to Talk]
Okay.

570
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:50,100
[Getting a Chance to Talk]

571
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:53,633
My friend meant well,

572
00:20:53,666 --> 00:20:56,266
and he did tell me beforehand
he was going to write that.

573
00:20:56,266 --> 00:20:57,466
But I honestly didn't expect

574
00:20:57,466 --> 00:20:59,666
[Unexpected]
it'd be read out loud

575
00:20:59,666 --> 00:21:00,733
[Unexpected]
in front of everyone.

576
00:21:00,733 --> 00:21:02,000
[Unexpected]
Plus, you're more introverted.

577
00:21:03,066 --> 00:21:04,866
I know it's gonna be hard on you.

578
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,366
And I couldn't control the situation

579
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,300
at the time.

580
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:12,700
I didn't know what to do.

581
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:13,900
So when you said,

582
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,533
"I choose not to answer,"

583
00:21:15,533 --> 00:21:18,833
I was like, "Sure. You don't have to."

584
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,700
I get it.

585
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,166
[Truly Sorry]

586
00:21:23,666 --> 00:21:24,266
The thing is,

587
00:21:24,266 --> 00:21:28,133
I've been trying
to process my emotions today.

588
00:21:28,133 --> 00:21:29,533
I really did feel

589
00:21:30,933 --> 00:21:32,466
a bit of pressure.

590
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:38,433
Because everyone was
kind of down at the time,

591
00:21:38,433 --> 00:21:40,933
and then that question
suddenly came up,

592
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:43,000
I was embarrassed
to be suddenly mentioned

593
00:21:43,033 --> 00:21:44,266
while sitting there

594
00:21:44,266 --> 00:21:46,866
and surrounded by people.

595
00:21:47,866 --> 00:21:48,300
Yeah.

596
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,033
And besides,

597
00:21:49,066 --> 00:21:51,700
we only sat next to each other
on the first day,

598
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:56,233
barely talked.

599
00:21:56,266 --> 00:21:58,533
[Don't Know Each Other Well]

600
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,466
I don't even really know

601
00:22:01,466 --> 00:22:04,066
what everyone's like yet.

602
00:22:05,266 --> 00:22:08,100
Other than what I saw on the Soul app,

603
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:09,700
[One of Their Few Interactions]
that sentence.

604
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,933
[One of Their Few Interactions]
When I saw it,

605
00:22:11,933 --> 00:22:13,233
I didn't comment right away.

606
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:15,666
[World's Biggest Potato.]
Isn't this my quote?

607
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:16,533
[I've liked putting up walls, but behind]
Isn't this my quote?

608
00:22:16,533 --> 00:22:17,266
[her mysterious mask is actually]
Isn't this my quote?

609
00:22:17,266 --> 00:22:18,100
[an innocent, adorable girl.]
Really?

610
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:20,233
[Xia Boyan. I put up walls,]
I said, "I put up walls."

611
00:22:20,266 --> 00:22:21,333
[yet choose to let you in.]
Comment, hurry.

612
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:22,000
It's possible.

613
00:22:22,733 --> 00:22:23,533
Hurry up!

614
00:22:23,533 --> 00:22:24,566
Comment first.

615
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:25,033
Hurry.

616
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:26,333
Have you commented?

617
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:28,000
Wait. I'm gonna wait for the last one.

618
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:33,466
But I guessed it was you.

619
00:22:33,466 --> 00:22:34,166
I asked,

620
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:36,933
"Was that meant
for someone in particular?"

621
00:22:36,933 --> 00:22:38,733
And you said, "Take a guess."

622
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:41,433
Then we didn't really talk after that.

623
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:43,533
Couldn't really talk, either.

624
00:22:43,533 --> 00:22:46,000
I just thought we
randomly paired up for the game,

625
00:22:46,033 --> 00:22:48,433
nothing more than that.

626
00:22:49,733 --> 00:22:50,433
So,

627
00:22:50,466 --> 00:22:53,700
I know that we all have
different personalities.

628
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:54,766
I really do.

629
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,933
But I was upset today

630
00:22:58,933 --> 00:23:05,166
because I kinda felt pressured

631
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:07,133
and embarrassed.

632
00:23:08,233 --> 00:23:10,733
When I feel embarrassed,

633
00:23:10,733 --> 00:23:12,966
I tend to feel down.

634
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,433
And you can see that all over my face.

635
00:23:15,433 --> 00:23:17,233
So I also want to apologize to you.

636
00:23:17,233 --> 00:23:19,466
[Feeling Sorry]
If I did something today

637
00:23:19,466 --> 00:23:20,666
that made you feel...

638
00:23:20,666 --> 00:23:22,300
No.

639
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,700
Nothing.

640
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:24,900
It's totally normal.

641
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:27,433
Okay.

642
00:23:30,133 --> 00:23:32,133
It's only day three.

643
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:35,700
We're all still testing the waters.

644
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,700
You're right. I totally get it.

645
00:23:38,466 --> 00:23:39,166
Yeah.

646
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:46,166
[Misunderstandings
ease away with the tide.]

647
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,566
[Moonlight spreads a safe distance]

648
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:48,966
[where the feeling's softer than love,]

649
00:23:48,966 --> 00:23:49,666
[deeper than friendship.]

650
00:23:49,866 --> 00:23:52,400
So what do you want
to talk to me about these two days?

651
00:23:52,433 --> 00:23:53,466
I don't really know.

652
00:23:56,933 --> 00:23:58,400
I'm pretty sentimental.

653
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,666
And I think everything I did,

654
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:04,533
like voting for you,

655
00:24:04,533 --> 00:24:06,733
was all my own choice.

656
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:09,500
I don't expect you
to do anything in return.

657
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:12,200
And when I start liking someone,

658
00:24:12,233 --> 00:24:15,366
I always observe them
from a distance first.

659
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,933
I don't want to create some illusion

660
00:24:17,933 --> 00:24:19,233
about what kind of person

661
00:24:19,266 --> 00:24:20,200
you might be for myself.

662
00:24:20,233 --> 00:24:21,433
I don't really know you yet.

663
00:24:22,033 --> 00:24:22,233
Yes.

664
00:24:22,233 --> 00:24:25,266
So I'll step back and just watch first.

665
00:24:25,266 --> 00:24:26,800
When the timing feels right,

666
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:29,733
we can really get to know each other.

667
00:24:30,733 --> 00:24:33,833
I think it's about enjoying the process,

668
00:24:33,866 --> 00:24:35,933
and going with it.

669
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:36,633
I agree.

670
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:39,200
[Slow down the paces]

671
00:24:39,233 --> 00:24:41,833
[and meet again at the right moment]

672
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:42,700
[and meet again at the right moment]
Take it slow.

673
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:44,766
[and meet again at the right moment]

674
00:24:44,833 --> 00:24:46,566
[and meet again at the right moment]
Wanna go back and play games?

675
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:47,200
[and meet again at the right moment]
Sure.

676
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,100
[and meet again at the right moment]

677
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:50,366
I was scared to 'death' this morning.

678
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:52,133
I was like, "Oh, no.

679
00:24:52,133 --> 00:24:53,633
I'm the one leaving."

680
00:24:53,666 --> 00:24:54,800
How could that be?

681
00:24:54,833 --> 00:24:56,533
You didn't think I'd leave?

682
00:24:56,533 --> 00:24:57,666
No, that's impossible.

683
00:24:57,700 --> 00:24:58,233
Why?

684
00:24:58,266 --> 00:24:59,333
Because I gave you many votes.

685
00:24:59,333 --> 00:25:00,200
[I gave you many Moonstones.]

686
00:25:00,266 --> 00:25:00,933
[I gave you many Moonstones.]
How many?

687
00:25:00,933 --> 00:25:01,600
[I gave you many Moonstones.]

688
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:02,500
Guess.

689
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,366
I'm not guessing.

690
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:06,933
What did you feel when you saw the list?

691
00:25:06,933 --> 00:25:07,533
Which list?

692
00:25:07,533 --> 00:25:08,666
The Danger Zone list.

693
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:12,633
If Autumn hadn't teamed up
with me yesterday,

694
00:25:13,633 --> 00:25:15,300
I probably would've just frozen there.

695
00:25:15,300 --> 00:25:16,600
I couldn't choose.

696
00:25:16,633 --> 00:25:19,700
I made my choice based on
how much time I'd spent...

697
00:25:19,700 --> 00:25:20,200
With that person.

698
00:25:21,233 --> 00:25:22,500
If there were too many aspects
to think about,

699
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:23,100
I'd get stuck.

700
00:25:23,100 --> 00:25:24,000
I'm terrible at making decisions.

701
00:25:25,100 --> 00:25:27,100
You don't have any questions for me?

702
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:28,133
Anything you're curious about?

703
00:25:28,133 --> 00:25:29,266
You're not overthinking anymore?

704
00:25:29,300 --> 00:25:30,700
I thought you'd be overthinking.

705
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:32,033
Not really.

706
00:25:32,066 --> 00:25:34,966
That phase already passed.

707
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:35,800
[That phase has passed.]
That phase already passed.

708
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:37,233
[That phase has passed.]
So it's like...

709
00:25:37,233 --> 00:25:40,300
The pieces finally fit.

710
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:41,200
Puzzle solved.

711
00:25:44,233 --> 00:25:45,533
Aren't you curious about my age?

712
00:25:45,533 --> 00:25:46,466
[Wanna know my age?]

713
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:47,433
I have a rough idea.

714
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,500
Didn't you say yesterday

715
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:50,400
that I was older than you?

716
00:25:50,433 --> 00:25:51,966
Yeah, that's my 'rough idea'.

717
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:52,933
[Age<Age]

718
00:25:53,033 --> 00:25:55,266
Do you think I'm older
or younger than you?

719
00:25:55,266 --> 00:25:56,600
Probably not much older than me.

720
00:25:57,533 --> 00:25:59,400
[Age>Age]

721
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:01,133
So you think I'm older?

722
00:26:04,933 --> 00:26:06,466
Remember what range I said was okay?

723
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:07,300
Up or down.

724
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:08,966
Right, the age gap you allowed

725
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,400
was pretty small.

726
00:26:12,066 --> 00:26:15,166
At most one year younger than me,

727
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:17,100
but older is fine.

728
00:26:17,100 --> 00:26:18,433
One or two years?

729
00:26:18,466 --> 00:26:20,500
You think you're
one or two years younger than me?

730
00:26:20,500 --> 00:26:22,133
Not necessarily.

731
00:26:23,433 --> 00:26:25,100
Oops, I just turned 18.

732
00:26:26,466 --> 00:26:27,333
You just turned 18?

733
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:28,900
Then I'm at junior high.

734
00:26:29,866 --> 00:26:31,500
What if I'm really younger than you?

735
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:32,333
In that case...

736
00:26:32,866 --> 00:26:35,400
This show's setup

737
00:26:35,433 --> 00:26:36,533
is so restrictive.

738
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:38,400
So age is not gonna be a problem.

739
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:39,933
So you think I'm older than you.

740
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:41,533
Doesn't matter.

741
00:26:43,466 --> 00:26:44,133
You only need to hear

742
00:26:44,133 --> 00:26:45,766
the last sentence I said.

743
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:47,333
We're like two bickering kids.

744
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:50,166
I kinda like it

745
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:51,600
when people say I'm mature.

746
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:53,600
I hate when they call me childish.

747
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:54,733
I think you're probably

748
00:26:54,733 --> 00:26:57,200
on the mature side for your age group.

749
00:26:57,233 --> 00:27:00,266
When we're closer, I might start
to show the playful side.

750
00:27:00,266 --> 00:27:03,200
Now, since we're
still figuring each other out,

751
00:27:03,233 --> 00:27:04,333
I come off a bit more mature.

752
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:07,700
Funny.

753
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:12,366
[Peeking]

754
00:27:12,433 --> 00:27:13,366
[Peeking]
Who's that?

755
00:27:13,400 --> 00:27:13,900
[Checking]

756
00:27:13,933 --> 00:27:14,533
[Checking]
Is that Huihui (Duan Danhui)?

757
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:15,133
[Checking]

758
00:27:15,266 --> 00:27:16,500
Yes, it is.

759
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:17,866
[Wandering]

760
00:27:17,900 --> 00:27:19,233
[Wandering]
Who's next to her?

761
00:27:19,266 --> 00:27:20,133
[Wandering]
Pan (Pan Xiaoyi).

762
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:33,800
So hard.

763
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:34,733
Tell me about it.

764
00:27:34,733 --> 00:27:36,466
I'm tired.

765
00:27:36,500 --> 00:27:37,500
Got anyone you like?

766
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:42,000
I feel like I've been observing

767
00:27:42,033 --> 00:27:43,666
[Outsider]
from the outside.

768
00:27:43,666 --> 00:27:44,700
[Outsider]
Why is that?

769
00:27:44,700 --> 00:27:46,166
Didn't get to interact with them much.

770
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,066
Have you tried to?

771
00:27:47,066 --> 00:27:48,766
Go interact.

772
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:50,333
I should've done that.

773
00:27:50,333 --> 00:27:51,066
Yeah.

774
00:27:51,733 --> 00:27:53,433
But there weren't many chances.

775
00:27:53,466 --> 00:27:54,533
What are you talking about?

776
00:27:54,533 --> 00:27:57,033
Weren't you just chatting
with Yao Qianyu?

777
00:27:57,066 --> 00:27:58,600
You said you two
were having a 'bro talk'.

778
00:27:58,633 --> 00:28:01,266
Then go find someone
who's not a 'bro' to talk to.

779
00:28:01,266 --> 00:28:01,933
When you're done chatting with her,

780
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:03,200
go talk to someone else.

781
00:28:04,133 --> 00:28:05,233
I don't know.

782
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:06,066
I just feel weird.

783
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:07,533
But hey,

784
00:28:07,533 --> 00:28:09,200
just try to make the best of the show.

785
00:28:09,233 --> 00:28:10,166
You gatta adapt

786
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,300
to the rules.

787
00:28:11,300 --> 00:28:12,100
Yeah.

788
00:28:17,666 --> 00:28:18,666
Man.

789
00:28:18,666 --> 00:28:19,333
With that kind of persistence,

790
00:28:19,333 --> 00:28:20,566
[The 'Culprit']
you'll succeed at anything.

791
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:21,266
[The 'Culprit']
Yeah.

792
00:28:21,333 --> 00:28:24,066
[Killing Anxiety with Physical Work]

793
00:28:24,300 --> 00:28:25,300
You're gonna talk to her again?

794
00:28:25,300 --> 00:28:26,533
Of course.

795
00:28:26,533 --> 00:28:27,866
I'll get you a yogurt.
You give it to her.

796
00:28:27,900 --> 00:28:28,566
Okay.

797
00:28:28,833 --> 00:28:30,166
[Yogurt = You Go]

798
00:28:30,233 --> 00:28:30,900
[Yogurt = You Go]
Here. Go.

799
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:32,700
[Showing Up]
Hey, I got you a yogurt.

800
00:28:32,700 --> 00:28:33,400
[Showing Up]

801
00:28:33,466 --> 00:28:34,566
[Offering Yogurt]
Thank you.

802
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:35,866
[Offering Yogurt]
Not much else on the island.

803
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:36,966
Thank you.

804
00:28:37,233 --> 00:28:38,033
I'll just put it here.

805
00:28:44,333 --> 00:28:48,033
[Finally, the day's almost over.]

806
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:54,066
The Moon of Affection has lit up.

807
00:28:54,066 --> 00:28:56,933
All islanders,
please head to the Moon of Affection

808
00:28:56,933 --> 00:29:00,000
for tonight's affection voting.

809
00:29:00,033 --> 00:29:03,066
Every sentiment flows like moonlight,

810
00:29:03,066 --> 00:29:06,266
and every affection makes
the moon phase fuller.

811
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:10,800
[Affection Voting
at the Moon of Affection]

812
00:29:11,466 --> 00:29:11,900
How many people

813
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:12,633
[Walking Huihui There]
did you vote for yesterday?

814
00:29:12,666 --> 00:29:13,733
[Walking Huihui There]
Three.

815
00:29:13,733 --> 00:29:14,833
[Walking Huihui There]
But you got the most votes.

816
00:29:14,866 --> 00:29:16,000
How many people
are you gonna vote for today?

817
00:29:16,033 --> 00:29:17,100
I don't want to tell you.

818
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:19,033
You'll find out later anyway.

819
00:29:19,066 --> 00:29:19,800
Okay.

820
00:29:23,666 --> 00:29:26,733
[Today's Votes: Four Moonstones]

821
00:29:30,900 --> 00:29:32,100
[Goes straight to...]

822
00:29:33,533 --> 00:29:37,766
[Duan Danhui
